---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const layers = [
  {
    number: '01',
    name: 'Sandbox',
    description: 'Isolated computers where agents can use files, a terminal, and a browser.',
    href: 'https://sandbox.tangle.tools/',
    link: 'Open Sandbox',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    name: 'Runtime',
    description: 'The execution loop that runs agent work and records what happened.',
    href: 'https://github.com/tangle-network/agent-runtime',
    link: 'View runtime source',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    name: 'Router',
    description: 'One API for model access, provider selection, and fallback.',
    href: 'https://router.tangle.tools/',
    link: 'Open Router',
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    name: 'Integrations',
    description: 'Controlled connections to the tools and systems an agent needs.',
    href: 'https://docs.tangle.tools/',
    link: 'Read the docs',
  },
  {
    number: '05',
    name: 'Observability',
    description: 'Traces and evidence for inspecting runs and comparing changes.',
    href: 'https://intelligence.tangle.tools/',
    link: 'Explore Intelligence',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is Tangle?"
  description="Tangle is an infrastructure company for AI agents, with a product lab and a research lab. Explore its five infrastructure layers and first packaged use case."
>
  <div class="definition-page">
    <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="definition-title">
      <div class="opening-inner">
        <h1 id="definition-title">What is Tangle?</h1>
        <p class="definition">Tangle is an infrastructure company for AI agents, with a product lab and a research lab.</p>
        <p class="opening-detail">Developers and teams use its infrastructure to run agents, connect the systems they need, and inspect the work. Tangle offers hosted infrastructure. On-premises hosting is planned and is not available today.</p>
        <div class="entry-points" aria-label="Choose how to explore Tangle">
          <a class="entry-primary" href="https://sandbox.tangle.tools/">Build with the infrastructure <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="entry-secondary" href="/#assistant-preview">See the hosted assistant preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="layers-section" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="layers-title">Five layers for agent work</h2>
        <p>These layers support the products Tangle builds and the infrastructure it sells.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="layer-list">
        {layers.map((layer) => (
          <li>
            <span class="layer-number" aria-hidden="true">{layer.number}</span>
            <h3>{layer.name}</h3>
            <p>{layer.description}</p>
            <a href={layer.href}>{layer.link} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="evaluation-note"><strong>Evaluation runs through the stack.</strong> Teams can test behavior in each layer and product. Evaluation is a capability across Tangle, not a sixth infrastructure layer.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="labs-section" aria-labelledby="labs-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="labs-title">Products and research use the infrastructure</h2>
        <p>Tangle builds on the same layers it offers to developers and teams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="labs-content">
        <div>
          <h3>Product lab</h3>
          <p>Hosted assistants are the first packaged use case. The hospitality guest-request assistant is in preview; its full request-to-resolution flow is still being tested with a design partner. Agent Builder helps developers build domain apps. Braid runs coding agents through a durable terminal client. Phone lines and vertical apps are further product work.</p>
          <a href="/#assistant-preview">Read about the assistant preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Research lab</h3>
          <p>Discovery and the software factory use Tangle infrastructure to investigate how agents run, learn from evidence, and improve under review.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/tangle-network">Explore Tangle source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .definition-page { background: #0c0b1d; color: #f5f5fb; }
  .opening { background: radial-gradient(ellipse 75% 70% at 78% 8%, #25215a 0, #0c0b1d 74%); border-bottom: 1px solid #30304c; }
  .opening-inner, .layers-section, .labs-section { max-width: 76rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: 2rem; padding-right: 2rem; }
  .opening-inner { padding-top: clamp(8rem, 12vw, 11rem); padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem); }
  h1, h2, h3, p { margin: 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3.8rem, 9vw, 8.5rem); line-height: .98; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.065em; }
  .definition { max-width: 58rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3.1vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .opening-detail { max-width: 48rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: #c7c9e1; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .entry-points { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .entry-points a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; min-height: 3.4rem; padding: .85rem 1.2rem; border: 1px solid #7778b5; border-radius: .5rem; color: #fff; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .entry-points a:hover, .entry-points a:focus-visible { background: #302c65; outline-offset: 3px; }
  .entry-primary { background: #4f46e5; border-color: #4f46e5 !important; }
  .entry-secondary { background: #1d1b38; }
  .layers-section, .labs-section { padding-top: 6rem; padding-bottom: 6rem; }
  .section-intro { max-width: 47rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .section-intro p { margin-top: 1rem; color: #c7c9e1; font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .layer-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid #444460; }
  .layer-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(9rem, 1fr) minmax(15rem, 2fr) minmax(9rem, auto); align-items: baseline; gap: 1.2rem; padding: 1.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #444460; }
  .layer-number { color: #a5aafc; font: 600 .85rem/1.4 monospace; }
  .layer-list h3 { font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .layer-list p { color: #c7c9e1; line-height: 1.55; }
  .layer-list a, .labs-content a { color: #bec1ff; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .25rem; }
  .layer-list a { justify-self: end; text-align: right; }
  .evaluation-note { max-width: 50rem; margin-top: 2rem; color: #c7c9e1; line-height: 1.65; }
  .evaluation-note strong { color: #f5f5fb; }
  .labs-section { border-top: 1px solid #30304c; }
  .labs-content { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem); }
  .labs-content > div { border-top: 2px solid #818cf8; padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .labs-content h3 { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .labs-content p { margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem; color: #c7c9e1; line-height: 1.65; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .opening-inner, .layers-section, .labs-section { padding-left: 1.25rem; padding-right: 1.25rem; }
    .layer-list li { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; gap: .5rem 1rem; }
    .layer-list h3 { grid-column: 2; }
    .layer-list p, .layer-list a { grid-column: 2; }
    .layer-list a { justify-self: start; text-align: left; margin-top: .3rem; }
    .labs-content { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .opening-inner { padding-top: 7rem; }
    .entry-points a { width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
